      <memberdef kind="function" id="MRTiff_8h_1ae4661697cb83e683195e70223e1f168f" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type><ref refid="include_2MRCMisc_2exports_8h_1a83dd8809128f2fbd49b5c39d59179d4a" kindref="member">MRC_API</ref> <ref refid="MRTiff_8h_1af973406beb1038c22c5342ae0d99a27e" kindref="member">MR_expected_MR_Raster_std_string</ref> *</type>
        <definition>MRC_API MR_expected_MR_Raster_std_string * MR_RasterLoad_fromTiff</definition>
        <argsstring>(const char *path, const char *path_end, const MR_RasterLoadSettings *settings)</argsstring>
        <name>MR_RasterLoad_fromTiff</name>
        <param>
          <type>const char *</type>
          <declname>path</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const char *</type>
          <declname>path_end</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const <ref refid="MRTiff_8h_1a8a32d017de76b733fb7da342370bbc72" kindref="member">MR_RasterLoadSettings</ref> *</type>
          <declname>settings</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>loads the first image of a .tiff file as a raster with one layer:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>gray, palette and RGB images keep the stored samples of any type (gray values, color indices or color components) as channels;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>libtiff decodes the other formats (gray with alpha, YCbCr, CMYK, less than 8 bits per sample, etc.) to four UInt8 channels of RGBA colors;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>the formats that libtiff cannot decode are read as stored too if each pixel has one sample or three or more interleaved samples of 8 to 64 bits, otherwise loading fails;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>the files compressed by the methods that libtiff does not support fail to load;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>the rows keep the stored order whatever the Orientation tag says, also in the decoded formats Generated from function <computeroutput>MR::RasterLoad::fromTiff</computeroutput>. Parameter <computeroutput>path</computeroutput> is a UTF-8 encoded filesystem path. Parameter <computeroutput>settings</computeroutput> is a single object. Parameter <computeroutput>settings</computeroutput> has a default argument: <computeroutput>{}</computeroutput>, pass a null pointer to use it. Never returns null. Returns an instance allocated on the heap! Must call <computeroutput><ref refid="expected__MR__Raster__std__string_8h_1a610dadc5a92d224ed1017725396d1cca" kindref="member">MR_expected_MR_Raster_std_string_Destroy()</ref></computeroutput> to free it when you&apos;re done using it. </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
